  "body": "As in every OS, files can be assigned to default applications to be open with. If I assign a raw file type to ART, then double clicking on it (or even right clicking and choosing \"open with ART\") doesn't open the file ready for editing.\n\nART is correctly launched but it defaults to opening the folder chosen in the settings, which might not be the one where the file is located and in any case no file is open.\n\nOn the other hand, if I launch ART from the terminal and pass the file as an argument, it correctly opens it, ready to be edited, which is the expected behaviour, as shown by `--help`.\n \nI haven't checked whether this is a MacOS only problem or it's also present in Gnome, KDE or even Windows.",
